@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@ Bring your own API keys — Gemini, and optionally GPT, Grok, or Claude — or r
 ## Features
 
 - **Dictate**: Record speech; the transcription inserts at the cursor when auto-paste is on, and is always copied to the clipboard. Use Gemini, OpenAI, or any audio-capable model on OpenRouter, your own OpenAI-compatible server (LiteLLM, Azure, …), or an on-device model offline. Offline, **Parakeet Ultra** is the recommended model: 25 European languages, German and English included, transcribed in a fraction of a second after Stop (about 0.1 s for a sentence, under a second for a minute without Glossary terms) at the accuracy of Whisper Large v3 Turbo, ~700 MB download. On-device models write the German layout commands "Doppelpunkt", "neuer Absatz" and "neue Zeile" as ":", a blank line and a line break, and the Punctuation setting "Only when spoken" (Settings → Dictate) drops the model's own punctuation so only spoken "Punkt", "Komma" (between digits a decimal comma: "3 Komma 5" is "3,5"), "Fragezeichen" and "Ausrufezeichen" are written, plus "Schrägstrich" as "/" (spoken-only); Whisper models stay available for other languages. Temperature and thinking effort are configurable for cloud models. Longer recordings start transcribing while you still speak — Gemini, OpenAI, Grok, and on-device Whisper — so pressing Stop only waits for the last chunk (Parakeet transcribes the whole recording after Stop, which is faster still). If a chunk fails, the app falls back to transcribing the full recording.
+- **Dictate Live**: Text at the cursor as you speak. Give **Dictate Live** a shortcut in Settings → General (none by default) or use the menu bar item: after each short pause, what you said since the last one appears at the cursor, transcribed offline by Parakeet Ultra with your Glossary. Text that is in is never rewritten, so you correct it as you go; ✕ stops the recording but leaves inserted text where it is. If another app comes to the front while you dictate, the text waits instead of landing there, and ends on the clipboard if you stay away. Needs Parakeet Ultra downloaded, an Apple silicon Mac and the Accessibility permission; direct-download build only. Fn can start Dictate Live instead of normal Dictate (Settings → General → Keyboard Shortcuts).
 - **Add Selection to Glossary**: Select a correctly spelled term anywhere — your practice software, a document, an email — and use the menu item or a shortcut you set in Settings → General (it has no default shortcut; direct-download build only). It is appended to the Glossary verbatim, with a duplicate check. No model is involved, which makes it the way to grow the Glossary while Offline Mode is on, where the model-driven learning paths (Smart Improvement, the typed-text learner) do not run.
 - **Offline Mode**: One switch (Settings → Privacy & Permissions, also offered during onboarding) that makes the app device-local: dictation runs on an on-device model (Parakeet Ultra or Whisper), requests the app itself builds are blocked at the network layer, and no transcript, prompt or audio sample is written to the usage log. Requests to your own machine or local network still work, so a Whisper server or Ollama on your network stays available. Downloading a Parakeet, Whisper or MLX model from Hugging Face still works (FluidAudio and WhisperKit use their own URLSessions, which the Offline Mode guard does not wrap — that download carries no content of yours; once downloaded, Parakeet loads with FluidAudio's own network switch shut and never re-downloads on its own; a failed load is reported, and Delete + Download in Settings is the repair). Dictate Prompt keeps working through an in-process MLX model (Qwen3 4B Instruct, downloads itself, no server needed) or a local Ollama / LM Studio server if you prefer to run your own. Offline MLX and HTTP-local models read plain text, so they take the text to edit from your clipboard — in the App Store build, copy the text yourself (⌘C) before you start dictating, since that build cannot copy the selection for you. Dictate Prompt also sends no earlier turns as history while it is on, so a note from the previous patient never travels with the next request. It also decodes greedily (temperature 0), so the same dictation is structured the same way every time, and checks every reply word by word against your dictation: words in the result that you did not dictate (headings, punctuation, segment formatting like L4/L5 and simple inflections aside) are listed in a "Not in your dictation" warning — shown even with popups off — while the text itself is pasted unchanged. Chat can run on the same offline MLX models; Read Aloud uses on-device macOS voices. Smart Improvement and the Google and Trello integrations have no on-device equivalent and stop working while it is on. Built for regulated dictation — patient findings, case notes — where "the recording never leaves this device" has to hold whatever else is configured.
 - **Anonymous usage statistics (opt-in, off by default)**: A switch in onboarding and Settings → Privacy & Permissions that, when you turn it on, sends a daily summary of counts to the developer — how often features were used and whether they worked, failure classes, which built-in models ran, which features were used (for example screenshots, chat integrations, AI-app requests), and which features are switched on. Never transcripts, prompts, replies, audio, the apps you paste into, or any identifier. "See exactly what is sent" shows the exact JSON; turning it off deletes anything queued. Unavailable in Offline Mode. The receiving server's code is in `server/telemetry/`.
